CNES is currently developing a new system allowing transmission of remote control and monitoring data (called ST²). As part of the digitalization projects, CNES-CSG wishes to improve and digitalize asset monitoring within Payload facilities S1, S5 and S3B. The objective is to use ST² in order to monitor EPCU assets as well transport and laboratories means and equipment. 
The type of systems and subsystems to be supervised is very extensive (Mechanical means [cranes, doors with inflatable seals, etc.], fluid means [gas distribution networks, etc.], mobile means [trailers, manlifts, etc.])
The input data will be the description of the supervision needs for each system.

The project will consist in : 
To define communication technologies/tools/materials to be implemented in order to allow data feedback;
To define the architecture of the interface system with the ST² project for the overall supervision and data exploitation by operators;
To implement the defined solution;
To test and qualify the system ;
Chosen solutions must be compliant with the existing network resources and with the security rules applicable to the CSG.

